+# Production main-thread evidence publisher — held Source
+
+Root runs `python -X utf8 -B .runtime/porting/SRC-05/ordinary-main-publication-prep-01/publish.py --packet <actual-packet-path>#<actual-SHA256>` only after independent Source acceptance and both actual production processes have closed. This preparation performs no publication, canonical edit, build, target execution, or Git action.
+
+The actual packet schema is `src05-production-main-thread-publication-inputs.v1`. Its mandatory full-reference keys are `actual_validation`, `Root_PE_acceptance`, `actual_execution_custody`, `actual_execution_outer_receipt`, `Root_factual_review`, and `Header_factual_review`. Optional `closed_executions` contains genuine completed standard recorder receipts; optional `opaque_lineage` contains exact small Source/proof objects. Neither list may contain an active publication directory or its unfinished logs. The publisher selects explicit references, never scans active publication directories.
+
+Both factual reviews use `src05-ordinary-main-production-factual-review.v1`, distinct `reviewer_role` values `Root` and `Header`, and exact `actual_custody`, `actual_validation`, `Source_snapshot` references. They require `full_process_input_Source_output_and_capture_custody_review_accepted:true`, `scientific_comparison_performed:false`, `whole_ordinary_PASS_claimed:false`, and `gates_updated:false`. Additional actual review details are retained. No prospective outcome, numerical result, or count is supplied here.
+
+The fixed fresh destination is `energyplus_porting_plan/evidence/SRC-05-production-main-thread`. The publisher authenticates all archived files in the genuine before/literal/final Source snapshots, all 3,931 current Source members, the two additions, and the 3,927 unchanged members. It publishes only the four changed Rust source paths and their held/actual before, proposal, semantic-diff, final, and formatter-diff bytes. Unrelated Rust source payloads are excluded; snapshot descriptors remain available and the selected closure explicitly does not claim transitive replayability. Historical canonical before identities resolve only through the exact application before archives. Native inherited BUILD aliases remain declared historical metadata in the complete Native before/provider proofs, never rebound to current Rust paths.
+
+The retained routine evidence includes the complete application workflow 01/02/03 ancestry, genuine Source/formatter reviews, four role-specific quality receipts and full logs, exact reported test totals including ignored tests, two Cargo JSON streams/artifact messages, PE header bytes and proof metadata, actual process receipts/logs, and both complete factual reviews. Actual binary hashes are checked against currently available Cargo artifacts but executable payloads are excluded. Input/weather/IDD/metadata/fixed-scope and all 45 guarded ordinary inputs are fully rehashed and represented by descriptors only.
+
+The genuine `7b63de51...` Native dispatcher baseline is a prerequisite, not a cross-engine result. Its complete before/custody/Root and Header factual/provider proofs, Native receipt/stdout, bounded Source preparations, address/disassembly proof logs, and historical alias metadata are selected recursively. Huge executable, map, object, library, DLL, debug, and weather payloads are excluded. Snapshot raw archives and frozen-artifact arrays do not expand into a new unrelated Source closure.
+
+Every produced file under the fixed D output root must still exist and match its full custody SHA256 and size at publication; the complete file inventory must match. Hashing and gzip copying stream through bounded buffers. The potentially multi-gigabyte NDJSON and ordinary output payloads stay on D, with `storage_available_at_publication:true` and `payload_published:false`. Their capture header/footer/count/status metadata is retained as recorded; no event values are parsed, no failed process or incomplete capture becomes a numerical success, and no full payload publication is implied.
+
+Selected evidence uses content-addressed raw objects or lossless full gzip for files at least 512 KiB. Existing published identical objects may be reused only after full stored-byte or decompressed-byte SHA256/size verification. All selected/current inputs and external payloads are rechecked after archival. The summary reports actual process exits, quality totals, complete external descriptors, and explicit limits. It writes no plan/card/checklist/HTML, changes no gates, infers no historical FP state, and claims no ordinary integration or scientific PASS.
